1.163.m:
Having bathed on the seventh [lunar day], if a man worships the Sun even once,
he uplifts seven ancestral lines and is glorified in the world of the Sun;
and accompanied by wealth, gold, and the like, it is equal to a bath of milk.

A bath with copper pots is deemed a hundred times better than with earthen pots;
with silver ones, the merit is one-fourth greater. Touching is higher than seeing;
worship is superior to touching, and higher than this is the bath of ghee.
